        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cam Clarke, Katsuhiro Otomo, Ryōhei Suzuki, Shunzō Katō, Izo Hashimoto, Anna Paquin, Maggie Nelson, Kirby Morrow, Garry Chalk, Ron Halder, Nicole Oliver\n- Works: Akira, Mosaic, Otomo's manga of the same name\n- Roles: voice actor, singer, director, producer, writer\n- Topics: animation, video games, science fiction\n\nFacts:\n- Cam Clarke was born on November 6, 1957.\n- Cam Clarke is an American voice actor and singer known for voice work in animation and video games.\n- Akira is a 1988 Japanese adult animated science fiction film.\n- Katsuhiro Otomo directed Akira.\n- Ryōhei Suzuki and Shunzō Katō produced Akira.\n- Katsuhiro Otomo and Izo Hashimoto wrote Akira.\n- Akira was based on Katsuhiro Otomo's manga of the same name.\n- Mosaic features Anna Paquin as the voice of Maggie Nelson.\n- Mosaic has supporting voice roles by Kirby Morrow, Cam Clarke, Garry Chalk, Ron Halder, and Nicole Oliver.",
